From 629f566da34690b057e2fd5c2fbe1068ec584457 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:42:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 118/118] mtk-ccci: incoming calls and the call list over MIPC

MT6858's NR17 modem firmware hands each incoming call to a MIPC client
for approval (CALL_APPROVE_INCOMING_CMD) and reports call progress only
as MIPC indications (CALL_STATUS_IND, CALL_EVENT_IND). The AT port gets
no RING, +CLIP, +EAIC or +ECPI, and +CLCC lists no calls, so an
incoming call rang at the caller and never reached ModemManager. The
stock RIL is such a MIPC client, on ttyCMIPC1. It sends its single
AT+EURCRPT=2 through its own MIPC AT tunnel; sent on ttyC0 instead, the
command made every PDN activation fail (+CME ERROR: 5847).

Add a MIPC message codec with unit tests, and an MMPortMipc that opens
the session (INTERNAL_TEST_REQ, INTERNAL_OPEN_REQ), matches each
confirmation to its request by transaction id and passes indications
and commands to handlers. When the modem has a MIPC port, the plugin
registers for incoming-call approval and the two call indications,
approves each incoming call (as the stock RIL does unless it has to
reject one), and reloads the call list from CALL_GET_CALL_STATUS on
every indication. With every change indicated, periodic +CLCC polling
is off, and the AT port's call reports only trigger a reload. Dialing,
answering and hanging up stay on the AT port.

The protocol layout follows the messages the modem exchanges with the
stock libmipc (16-byte header, 4-byte TLV headers, 8-byte alignment)
and was checked against the modem on a JP2601.
